<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="JON" style="id"/>
  <para style="h">Yunusa</para>
  <para style="toc2">YUN</para>
  <para style="toc1">Yunusa</para>
  <para style="mt">Junusa</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="JON 1"/>
  <para style="s">Nabi Junusa ma sɔn Alla la kuma ma</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JON 1:1"/>Nba, lon do rɔ, Allabatala kumara Amitayi dencɛ Nabi Junusa yɛ. <verse eid="JON 1:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JON 1:2"/>A ka a fɔ ko: «I wuli! I ye sila mira i kɔrɔ. I ye wa Ninibe so ba kɔndɔ ka ye mɔɔilu jalakikan fɔ ii yɛ, baa ii ye kojuu mɛnilu kɛla, nde ka woilu lɔn.» <verse eid="JON 1:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JON 1:3"/>Kɔni Nabi Junusa ma sɔn ka wa Ninibe. A ka Tarasisi sila mira ka wa ko a ye a mataala Allabatala la ka bɔ a ɲakɔrɔ. A sera Jafa so kɔndɔ ka wa kɔɔji dala ye. A ka kulunba do tɛrɛn ye, mɛn watɔ Tarasisi. A ka kulunba tɛɛ sara bɔ, ka don kulunba kɔndɔ. A ni kulunkɔndɔ mɔɔilu wara kɔɔji ka a fɔ ko ii ye wala Tarasisi. Nabi Junusa ye a fɛ ka a mataa Allabatala la ka bɔ a ɲakɔrɔ.<verse eid="JON 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JON 1:4"/>Kɔni Allabatala ka fɔɲɔ ba lana kɔɔji kan. Fɔɲɔ bonyara fɔɔ kulunba tɛrɛ ye tiɲan ko rɔ. <verse eid="JON 1:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JON 1:5"/>Kulunkɔndɔ baaradenilu silanda kojuuya. Ii kelen kelenna bɛɛ ka a maari madiya ko wo ye ii kisi. Ii ka kulunkɔndɔ doninilu lafili kɔɔji rɔ sa kulunba ri fɛya kɔɔji kan. Wo ka a tɛrɛn Nabi Junusa ra jii kulunba kɔndɔ. A tɛrɛ ye sunɔɔla bakɛ. <verse eid="JON 1:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JON 1:6"/>Kulun naborila wara a tɛrɛn ye ka a kan nabɔ a ma ko: «Nfenna i lani sunɔɔ rɔ? I wuli! I ye i maari madiya! Tumado wo ri kininkinin an na ko la ka an kisi sa an kana faa.»<verse eid="JON 1:6"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JON 1:7"/>Kɔ fɛ, ii ka a fɔ i ɲɔɔn yɛ ko: «An ye a kalabe kɛ ka a lɔn mɛn ka kojuu ɲin nase an ma.» Ii ka a kalabe kɛ. Kala ka Nabi Junusa mira. <verse eid="JON 1:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JON 1:8"/>Ii ka Nabi Junusa maɲininka ko: «Yon ye kojuu ɲin nasela an ma? Ile don, i la baara ye nfen di? I bɔni mi? I ye jamana ɲuman de mɔɔ ri? Siya ɲuman ye i ri?» <verse eid="JON 1:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JON 1:9"/>Nabi Junusa ka ii jabi: «Heburu le nde ri. N ye Maari Allabatala le batola, sankolo Maari, mɛn ka kɔɔji ni duukolo dan.» <verse eid="JON 1:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JON 1:10"/>Ii silanda kojuuya kuma wo la, ka a maɲininka wo rɔ ko: «I ka ko suu ɲuman de kɛ?» Baa Nabi Junusa tun ka a fɔ ii yɛ kɔrɔman ko a boritɔla le ka bɔ Allabatala ɲakɔrɔ.<verse eid="JON 1:10"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JON 1:11"/>Nba, kɔɔji tora lamaala fɔɔ ka tamin fɔlɔma kan. Wo rɔ, ii ka a fɔ Nabi Junusa yɛ ko: «An ye nfen kɛ i la sa kɔɔji ri a masuma an naminin dɔ?» <verse eid="JON 1:11"/><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JON 1:12"/>Nabi Junusa ka a fɔ ko: «Ai ye n mira ka n nafili kɔɔji rɔ. Wo wa kɛ, kɔɔji ri a masuma ai laminin dɔ, baa n ka a lɔn ko fɔɲɔ ba ɲin wulini ai kanma nde le la ko rɔ.»<verse eid="JON 1:12"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JON 1:13"/>Wo bɛɛ ni a ta, kulunkɔndɔ baaradenilu ka kulun bori kɛ ii fanka bɛɛ la, sa ii ri gbere masɔrɔn. Kɔni ii ma se, baa kɔɔji tora lamaala fɔɔ ka tamin fɔlɔma kan. <verse eid="JON 1:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JON 1:14"/>Ii ka Allabatala matara wo rɔ ko: «Ɛɛ, Allabatala. I jaandi! Ni an ka cɛɛ ɲin nafili kɔɔji rɔ ka a faa, i kana an datiɲan. Ni an ka a faa ka a tɛrɛn a ye mɔɔ jalakibali le ri, i kana an jalaki a faa rɔ, baa, Allabatala, ko mɛn wa diya i yɛ, i ye wo le kɛla.» <verse eid="JON 1:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JON 1:15"/>Wo rɔ, ii ka Nabi Junusa mira ka a lafili kɔɔji rɔ. Kɔɔji masumara i kɔrɔ. <verse eid="JON 1:15"/><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JON 1:16"/>Kulunkɔndɔ baaradenilu ka wo yen tuma mɛn na, ii silanda Allabatala yɛ kosɛbɛ. Ii ka saraka bɔ ka Allabatala sɔ wo la, ka dakan ta a yɛ.<verse eid="JON 1:16"/></para>
  <chapter eid="JON 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="JON 2"/>
  <para style="s">Nabi Junusa ka Alla matara kɔɔji kɔrɔ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JON 2:1"/>Awa, Allabatala ka jɛɛ ba do lana mɛn ka Nabi Junusa lakunun. Nabi Junusa ka tele sawa ni su sawa kɛ jɛɛ kɔndɔ. <verse eid="JON 2:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JON 2:2"/>Ka a to jɛɛ kɔndɔ, Nabi Junusa ka a Maari Allabatala tara.<verse eid="JON 2:2"/></para>
  <para style="q">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="JON 2:3"/>A ka a fɔ ko:</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:3">«Allabatala, ka n to tɔrɔya ba rɔ, n ka i matara.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:3">I ka n jabi.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:3">Ka n to lakira rɔ saya rɔ, n kulera dɛmɛnni ko rɔ.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:3">I ka n namɛn.<verse eid="JON 2:3"/></para>
  <para style="q">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="JON 2:4"/>I ka n nafili kɔɔji rɔ,</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:4">fɔɔ kɔɔji dun ba kɔrɔ.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:4">Kɔɔji ka n naminin fan bɛɛ rɔ.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:4">I ka kɔɔji kuru ba mɛnilu lana,</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:4">woilu bɛɛ lara n kan.<verse eid="JON 2:4"/></para>
  <para style="q">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JON 2:5"/>N tɛrɛ ye a fɔla n jɛrɛ ma ko i ra n gbɛn ka n bɔ i ɲakɔrɔ.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:5">Kɔni n lani a la n di i la bon sɛniman yen ikɔ tuun.<verse eid="JON 2:5"/></para>
  <para style="q">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="JON 2:6"/>Kɔɔji ka n natunun ka n na ɲenemaya masilan.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:6">N jiira fɔɔ kɔɔji dun ba kɔrɔ.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:6">Kɔɔjikɔrɔ binilu mɔrɔnmɔrɔnni tɛrɛ n kun ma.<verse eid="JON 2:6"/></para>
  <para style="q">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JON 2:7"/>N jiira fɔɔ koyinkɛilu sen kɔrɔ kɔɔji kɔrɔ.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:7">N sera suilu la jamana rɔ. A da bɛɛ sɔɔra n ma kadawu.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:7">Kɔni ile, n Maari Allabatala,</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:7">i ka n kɛndɛ layɛlɛ lakira kɔndɔ.<verse eid="JON 2:7"/></para>
  <para style="q">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="JON 2:8"/>N Maari Allabatala, ka a to dɔɔni n tun di sa,</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:8">n miriya sera i ma.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:8">I ka n na matarali kan namɛn</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:8">i la bon sɛniman kɔndɔ.<verse eid="JON 2:8"/></para>
  <para style="q">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JON 2:9"/>Mɔɔ mɛnilu ye batofen ɲatɔnɔntanilu batola,</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:9">woilu ri bɔnɔ i la kaninteya rɔ.<verse eid="JON 2:9"/></para>
  <para style="q">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JON 2:10"/>Kɔni nde ri kalaman bɔ i yɛ ka i tando,</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:10">ka saraka di i ma.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:10">N ka dakan mɛn ta i yɛ, n di wo mafa.</para>
  <para style="q" vid="JON 2:10">Allabatala, ile kelen pe le ri se mɔɔ kisila.»<verse eid="JON 2:10"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JON 2:11"/>Awa, Allabatala kumara jɛɛ ba yɛ. Wo rɔ, jɛɛ ba ka Nabi Junusa labɔ gbere ma.<verse eid="JON 2:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="JON 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="JON 3"/>
  <para style="s">Nabi Junusa wara Ninibe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JON 3:1"/>Allabatala kumara Nabi Junusa yɛ a siɲa filana rɔ. <verse eid="JON 3:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JON 3:2"/>A ka a fɔ ko: «I ye i wuli ka wa Ninibe so ba kɔndɔ. N wa mɛn fɔ i yɛ, i ye wo lase Ninibekailu ma.» <verse eid="JON 3:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JON 3:3"/>Wo rɔ, Nabi Junusa wulira ka wa Ninibe, ikomin Allabatala ka a fɔ a yɛ ɲa mɛn ma. Ninibe tɛrɛ ye so ba le ri, mɔɔ ri tele sawa taama kɛ mɛn kɔndɔ. <verse eid="JON 3:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JON 3:4"/>Nabi Junusa seni Ninibe, a donda so kɔndɔ ka tele kelen kɛ taamala, ka ban ka ye mɔɔilu kawandi ko: «Yani tele binaanin, gbalo ba ri kɛ Ninibe.» <verse eid="JON 3:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JON 3:5"/>Alla ka mɛn fɔ Ninibekailu yɛ ka fara Nabi Junusa la, ii lara wo la. Ii ka a fɔ ko bɛɛ ye sun don ka landa faanin bila ii kan na, denilu ni mɔɔbailu bɛɛ. <verse eid="JON 3:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JON 3:6"/>Nba, wo kibaro sera Ninibe mansa ma tuma mɛn na, a ka i wuli a la mansaya siifen dɔ ka a la mansaya faanin bɔ a kan na. A ka landa faanin bila a kan na ka i sii buurigbɛ rɔ. <verse eid="JON 3:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JON 3:7"/>Wo kɔ, a ka mɔɔilu lɔ kelalasela Ninibekailu ma ko: «Mansacɛ ni a la ɲɛmɔɔilu ka a fɔ ko tɔn da sii mɔɔilu ni kolofenilu bɛɛ ma, nisiilu ni saailu ni bailu kɔnin. Ii si kana dɔɔnnin kɛ. Ii si kana ii min. <verse eid="JON 3:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JON 3:8"/>Mɔɔilu bɛɛ ye landa faanin bila ii kan na, ka do sidi kolofenilu bɛɛ kan na. Mɔɔ kelen kelenna bɛɛ ye Alla matara a fanka bɛɛ la. Bɛɛ ye a ban a sɔn juu rɔ, ka kojuu kɛ boloka. <verse eid="JON 3:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JON 3:9"/>Baa, yon ka a lɔn? Tumado ko Alla ri a la bolorabɛn yɛlɛman an kanma ka a ban a la mɔnɛ ba rɔ, kosa an kana faa.»<verse eid="JON 3:9"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="JON 3:10"/>Alla ka a yen mɛn kɛ ko Ninibekailu ra nimisa ka ii la kojuuilu boloka, a ka a miriya yɛlɛman. A ka masilannikan mɛn fɔ ii yɛ ko a kɛtɔ gbalo ba lala ii kan, a ka wo to ye.<verse eid="JON 3:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="JON 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="JON 4"/>
  <para style="s">Nabi Junusa mɔnɛra Alla la hina rɔ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JON 4:1"/>Wo ma diya Nabi Junusa yɛ fewu. A mɔnɛra kosɛbɛ. <verse eid="JON 4:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JON 4:2"/>A ka Allabatala matara ko: «Aa, Allabatala, ka n to n na jamana kɔndɔ fɔlɔ, a miriya tɛrɛ ye n na ko i ri a kɛ ten. Wo le ka a kɛ, n ka n kaliya ka n bori ka wa Tarasisi. Baa n tun ka a lɔn fewu ko i ye Alla le ri, mɛn na kininkinin ni ɲumaya ka bon kosɛbɛ. I ti mɔnɛla jona. I ye mɔɔilu kaninna kojuuya. I wa masilannikan mɛnilu fɔ, i rabɛnni tuma bɛɛ ka woilu to ye. <verse eid="JON 4:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JON 4:3"/>Allabatala, sisen, i ye n bɔ duunuɲa rɔ yan, baa saya fisa n yɛ ka tamin ɲenemaya la.» <verse eid="JON 4:3"/><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JON 4:4"/>Allabatala ka Nabi Junusa jabi: «A ye di? I jɔ ye mɔnɛ rɔ wa?»<verse eid="JON 4:4"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="JON 4:5"/>Nba, Nabi Junusa bɔra Ninibe so kɔndɔ, ka wa i sii telebɔ rɔ. A ka gbaa do lɔ ye, ka i sii wo kɔrɔ lulen na ka makɔnɔni kɛ, baa a ye a fɛ ka a yen ko mɛn tamintɔ so kɔndɔ. <verse eid="JON 4:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JON 4:6"/>Wo tuma, Maari Allabatala ka fɛɛjuu do lafɛrɛn ka yɛlɛ Nabi Junusa kun na ka lulen di a ma, ka a bɔ a la niilafin dɔ. Nabi Junusa sɛwara fɛɛjuu wo la kosɛbɛ. <verse eid="JON 4:6"/><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JON 4:7"/>Wo duusa gbɛ sɔɔma da la, Alla ka tunbu do lana. Tunbu wo donda fɛɛjuu rɔ ka a dɔɔn ka a ja. <verse eid="JON 4:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JON 4:8"/>Tele yɛlɛra tuma mɛn na, Alla ka fɔɲɔ ba kalaman nana ka bɔ telebɔ rɔ. Tele gbara Nabi Junusa kun na kojuuya fo a betɔ le tɛrɛ. A tɛrɛ ye a fɛ ka sa. A ka a fɔ ko: «Saya kɔni ka fisa n ma ka tamin ɲenemaya kan.» <verse eid="JON 4:8"/><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JON 4:9"/>Alla ka Nabi Junusa maɲininka ko: «A ye di? I jɔ ye mɔnɛ rɔ fɛɛjuu ja ko rɔ wa?» Nabi Junusa ka a fɔ ko: «N kɛ! N jɔ ye a rɔ! N da mɔnɛ haan ka n sɔn saya ma.» <verse eid="JON 4:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JON 4:10"/>Allabatala ka a fɔ ko: «Fɛɛjuu ni wo hina ye i la. I don ma baara si kɛ a la, mɛn di a labonya. A fɛrɛnda su fɔlɔ rɔ ka ja su filana rɔ. <verse eid="JON 4:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JON 4:11"/>I ye a fɛ nde kana kininkinin Ninibekailu ma, so belebele wo kɔndɔ mɔɔ waa kɛmɛ a ni waa muwan mɛnilu mɛn ti se bolokinin ni bolomaran faranfasila, kolofen siyaman ba wo ma jate ma lɔn.»<verse eid="JON 4:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="JON 4"/>
</usx>
